<!-- The Halo 3-style SCOREBOARD (Menu style Halo 3, menus.scoreboard: the settings panel's Game >
Menus > Scoreboard), in the place of the game's own scores while Back (the Vita's SELECT) is held
in a multiplayer game - local and split screen, System Link, ad hoc, online, a dedicated server's or
a PC's (crossplay) -, each player's own in their view. Built into each level's map (ingame.txt):
pause.xml's fonts and pictures. Held, it is drawn over the game without being open (the player plays
on: menu_functions.c "port h3 scoreboard", ui_widget.c ui_widget_port_held_screen_show): the game
type on the map, the score to win and the time left in the title strip; a team game's teams each
under a band of the team's colour with its score (the leading team first), a free for all's players
in one list, ranked as the game's own scores rank them; each player's nameplate in their colour (their
team's), name, score, kills, deaths, assists and ping bars (the latency meter's, network_distributed.c:
the host's table on a joined machine), this machine's rows lit, a crown on the host's, the party's
mark, the tester's small flame (only where the flame itself shows: its proof checked here), BOT on a
bot's; the dead and those out of lives dimmed. Triangle (or a tap) while it is held opens it as a
screen of the player's own (scoreboard/screen, open: the D-pad, the stick, L and R, a drag on the
touch screen scroll it; Cross on a player: their options - MUTE CHAT, ADD FRIEND or the friend's
state, KICK for the game's host alone; Circle closes). Split screen's views have the smaller
scoreboard/split, held only. The rows are read a few times a second, not every frame. The art is this
folder's own (tools/halo3_menu_art.py). -->
<menus>
